extraction_notes: "WB9 South America 2 printed 55-56 (cache p055-p056, page_offset 0). Printed 55 checked against a 110 dpi render. No pucara-mind-mage class was in production on 2026-09-25; the id is prefixed because mind-mage (Palladium Fantasy) exists. || XP: the Larhold Shaman, Pucara Mind Mage and Sun Priest ladder on printed 192, read off a render; lower bounds 0 / 2,051 / 4,101 / 8,251 / 16,501 / 24,601 / 34,701 / 49,801 / 69,901 / 95,001 / 130,101 / 180,201 / 230,301 / 280,401 / 340,501. In a pairing the occupation''s ladder wins over the race''s. || GROUP: psychic - a master psionic trained in special schools, which is the group every mind-mage-shaped O.C.C. carries. || RACE: the block is headed O.C.C. but its abilities say the character has all the powers and bonuses of the Pucara race, and the text calls these the race''s most powerful psychics; stored as race_restrictions only pucara-red-giant. So this class is written as the ADDITION to that race and deliberately restates nothing the race supplies: attribute dice, M.D.C., P.P.E., Horror Factor, the +4 vs magic and +5 vs horror factor, the natural abilities, the stone powers and the equipment all come from the R.C.C. (equipment_starting, special_abilities, natural_abilities and bonuses are all summed across a pairing, so restating them would double them). Standard Equipment prints Same as the Pucara R.C.C., so no equipment_starting is stored. No starting money is printed by either. No sdc_base or mdc_base is stated here: the race''s mdc_base always applies because the class cannot be taken without it. men_of_arms: false is stated because every O.C.C. with neither pool must carry the line; the book''s section heading is Forces of Darkness, not a men-of-arms heading, and the class is a psychic, so the core 1D6 is the reading (it can only matter played without the race, which race_restrictions forbids). || PSIONICS: master. Three powers from each of Sensitive, Physical and Healing and two Super at level one (11 picks, four starting groups); two more from any category every level from 2 (schedule entries 2-15). The Mind Melter restriction the book invokes is the one on Mind Wipe, Psi-Sword and Mentally Possess Others, not before third level; expressed as a Super except on the starting group and the level-2 entry. I.S.P. 4D6x10 + M.E., +15 per level. Merged with the race: the tier ties at master so the occupation''s isp_base, starting groups and schedule replace the race''s, which is what the book''s Enhanced headings mean. || SKILLS: the O.C.C. Skills repeat the race''s list plus Demon and monster lore (+10%, catalog Lore: Demons & Monsters 25+10) and swap Hand to Hand: Expert for Martial Arts. Named skills are held once across a pairing, so they are restated for the sheet; the two CHOICE groups the race already grants (Language: one of choice +15%, W.P. two of choice) are NOT restated, because choice groups from both halves are not merged and restating them would give two languages and four W.P.s. Hand to Hand: Martial Arts is granted and replaces the race''s Expert (a later grant wins). The book prints no upgrade sentence for this class, so no hand_to_hand block is stored; the race''s block (Martial Arts or Assassin for one pick) is what a pairing then shows. || RELATED: the book again prints R.C.C. Related Skills: nine, plus two at levels 3 and 6 and one at 8, 10, 12 and 14. Same list as the race except Espionage is Wilderness Survival and Detect Ambush only (no tracking or camouflage), Military none, and Rogue has no +2. Secondary: six, same limits without the bonuses."
